{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on bfbf6286 (U1): D1 yes, the in-place form changes uri, release and presentation, and nothing else. D2 yes, a changed publisher is refused in both forms. D3 yes, item N ends in the successor's creation entry: never two active, never none; U2 owns the moved archive stop position and its red. D4 yes, U1 scopes red (d) to upgrade-application; the install guard for a second install of the same application is a later request, after U4. D5 yes, U1 carries the new creation family (Register 29, Directory 28, Rules 16) with every pin, relation, seal and generated declaration it moves; the review lists them. F5 accepted: the trust check runs as the fetch-application outcome, and a refused answer changes nothing. Coupling accepted: no deployment of U1 to any room Worker until U2 lands; U1 lands on main without a deployment, and the deployment carries U1 and U2 together. State the Durable Object cost of one upgrade (the fetch operation) in the rate section.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}